course: dictionary
lesson: 14885
title: Recitation: saying words from memory
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A recitation is when you say a poem, speech or piece of writing out loud from memory. You do not read it from a page. Often other people are listening, and they are called the audience.
explain: «Our class held a poetry recitation in the hall, and every child said a poem by heart.» The clues are "said" and "by heart": the children spoke without reading, so recitation means saying words aloud from memory.
explain: Recitation can also mean a long spoken list of facts or events, said one after another. «The guide gave a recitation of the castle's kings and queens, from the first to the last.» Nobody is reading a poem here. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A recitation is a noun. It can be a poem, a speech, a piece of writing, or a list of facts.
fact: «Recitation» means saying a poem, speech or piece of writing aloud from memory, often in front of an audience.
fact: In church, people often join together in the recitation of a prayer or psalm, saying it aloud.
fact: In schools, recitation competitions help pupils learn rhythm and speak clearly.
fact: Recitation of the Quran is also a skilled art in religious life.
exercise: «The children gave a recitation of their favourite poems.» What is a recitation here? | *Saying poems aloud from memory | Silently reading poems to themselves | Drawing pictures of the poems | Writing a letter to a friend
exercise: «The guide gave a long recitation of the kings and queens, one after another.» What does recitation mean here? | A quiet picture of a castle | *A long spoken list of facts, said one after another | A song sung by the whole school | A game played with a ball
exercise: «In church, everyone joined in the recitation of the prayer.» How were the people saying the prayer? | *Aloud and together | Whispered, one person at a time | Silently and alone | Written on a card and handed round
test: «Mia said her poem from memory at the recitation.» What does recitation mean? | *Saying something aloud from memory | Painting the school hall | Drawing a picture of a poem | Reading from a book with the lights off
test: Which activity is a recitation? | Reading a poem aloud while looking at the page | *Saying a speech from memory in assembly | Writing a poem in your exercise book | Copying a list from the board
exam: Which sentence uses recitation correctly? | I went to the recitation to buy bread | The cat had a recitation in the garden | Recitation is a bright colour of paint | *The class held a recitation competition, where pupils said poems from memory
